# French texts of Mitsuki's park scene (assets/mitsuki/park). Each line: "original" = "translation".
language fr "Français"

"The park" = "Le parc"
"MITSUKI!!" = "MITSUKI !!"
"You came... you actually came..." = "Tu es venue... tu es vraiment venue..."
"I said ten minutes. It was twelve." = "J'ai dit dix minutes. Il en a fallu douze."
"I was so scared. They were everywhere..." = "J'avais si peur. Ils étaient partout..."
"I know. You stayed put. You did well." = "Je sais. Tu n'as pas bougé. C'est bien."
"Don't let go yet, okay?" = "Ne me lâche pas encore, d'accord ?"
"...I won't. Come. Let's sit down." = "...Promis. Viens. Asseyons-nous."
"Your hands are always so cold." = "Tes mains sont toujours si froides."
"Yours are always warm. It evens out." = "Les tiennes sont chaudes. Ça s'équilibre."
"Hey... can I tell you something?" = "Dis... je peux te dire un truc ?"
"Mhm." = "Mhm."
"Ever since... that day, I can't sleep." = "Depuis... ce jour-là, je ne dors plus."
"Something sits on my chest at night." = "La nuit, quelque chose pèse sur ma poitrine."
"I thought if I said it out loud..." = "Je pensais que si je le disais..."
"...Shh. You're safe now." = "...Chut. Tu es en sécurité maintenant."
"It's here. It's always been here..." = "C'est là. Ça a toujours été là..."
"MITSUKIII!!" = "MITSUKIII !!"
"...Hina." = "...Hina."
"...Give her back." = "...Rends-la-moi."
"...A knight. With a shield. On our street. Sure. Why not." = "...Un chevalier. Avec un bouclier. Dans notre rue. Bien sûr. Pourquoi pas."
"...There's no way someone built a snowman in the middle of the night." = "...Personne ne construit un bonhomme de neige en pleine nuit."
"That ball... Hina said a Christmas ball. Give it here." = "Cette boule... Hina parlait d'une boule de Noël. Donne-la-moi."
"Let go...! It won't let go!" = "Lâche...! Il ne lâche pas !"
"...A shadow. It got away." = "...Une ombre. Elle s'est enfuie."
"And you're just a snowman again. ...A happy one." = "Et te revoilà simple bonhomme de neige. ...Un joyeux."
"He looks happier now. ...What a night." = "Il a l'air plus heureux maintenant. ...Quelle nuit."
"Snowman" = "Bonhomme de neige"
